2. Step 10: "What is the status of the task?" → matched bare "status" in task_status regex → returned memory recall instead of LLM

I already fixed Step 10 by narrowing the task_status regex. Now I need to fix Step 2.

The Step 2 issue is: when the owner says "Sí, yo te autorizo. La quiero ahora." but there's no pending action (because readOnlyAuthorized was already true from prior test runs), the approval signal is detected but there's no activeAction to resolve. The code at line 6192 checks `if (approvalSignal !== 'neutral' && activeAction)` — if there's no activeAction, it skips the approval block entirely. Then the message gets classified and falls through to the LLM because it doesn't match any property keywords.

The fix: When approval is detected but there's no active action, AND the owner has readOnlyAuthorized=true, re-execute the last completed read-only action. Or better: when approval is detected with no active action, check if the last completed action was a read-only property action and re-execute it.

